  "query_preview": "(This evening through Sunday)...\nIssued at 222 PM EDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nQuiet weather will continue for most of the next week, with the only \nchance for rain in the forecast coming Saturday night and next \nSunday.\n\nNorthwest flow aloft will continue until next weekend. One cold \nfront will exit the area by this evening. A shortwave will bring \nanother cold front through on Wednesday, but this front won't have \nany moisture to work with as Gulf moisture will be confined to the \nfar southern USA. Most of the cooler air with this front will be \nconfined to areas north and east of central Indiana.\n\nTemperatures will be a little cooler on Monday, with the coolest \ntemperatures expected Monday night. High pressure providing clear \nskies, light winds, and a dry atmosphere will bring temperatures \ndown into the upper 30s to lower 40s for most areas. Blended \nguidance looks too warm given ideal radiational cooling, so the \naforementioned numbers are cooler than that guidance suggests. Some \npatchy frost is possible in favored cold areas.\n\nOtherwise, the dry atmosphere and drying ground will allow for \nlarger diurnal temperature swings. Readings will average above \nnormal, with highs in the 70s to around 80 and lows generally in the \nupper 40s to lower 50s for Tuesday through Saturday.\n\nThese conditions will allow for afternoon minimum humidity in the 30 \nto 40 percent range, with some areas possible getting below 30 \npercent. This will bring an increase in fire concerns, but \nlight winds will mitigate the threat.\n\nSaturday night into next Sunday, an upper low moving into the area \nmay bring some scattered showers. Temperatures will remain warm \nSunday.",
